            Now compare those numbers with your fixtures. A standard showerhead is 2.5 GPM or less, and many newer ones are 2.0 or 1.8. A kitchen tap runs at about 1.5. A typical household wants one shower plus one tap at the same time, about 4 GPM. In a warm climate a 24 to 27 kW unit covers that easily. With 40°F water, even 36 kW is only just there. Our <a href="/what-size-tankless-water-heater-do-i-need/" class="text-[#1E90FF] font-bold hover:underline">tankless sizing guide</a> walks through the calculation fixture by fixture.
