        <div id="electrical" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            5. Breakers, Wire and Your Service Panel
          </h2>

          <p>
            Whole-house electric tankless units split their heating elements across several circuits, each with its own double-pole breaker and its own wire run back to the panel. That is why the specifications read like 3 x 40 A. It means three separate 40 amp, 240 volt circuits, not one. Add the amps together to get the total draw, and compare that with the size of your main service, usually printed on the main breaker at the top of the panel.
          </p>

