        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Electric tankless works brilliantly when the numbers fit. Check your coldest incoming water temperature, add up what you run at once, and get a load calculation before you buy. For a one- or two-bathroom house in a moderate or warm climate, the Stiebel Eltron Tempra 24 Plus is our pick, and the EcoSmart ECO 27 is the value choice where the panel can spare 112.5 amps.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            In a cold climate, go up to the Tempra 29 Plus or the ECO 36 only if your service can carry it, and compare that total cost honestly with a heat pump or gas unit. For a remote bathroom or kitchen, the EcoSmart ECO 11 is the simplest fix of all.
          </p>
